# Frontend Folder Structure

Keep UI code in this layout. Do not invent parallel folders (`screens/`, `providers/`, `theme/`).

```
lib/
├── views/<feature>/          # screens (*_view.dart)
├── widgets/<type>/           # reusable UI (button/, text/, container/, …)
├── controllers/<feature>/    # GetxControllers
├── core/
│   ├── constants/            # AppColors, AppImages, AppStrings
│   ├── utils/                # AppTheme, AppSize, validators, …
│   ├── extensions/
│   ├── bindings/
│   └── services/
├── models/
└── routes/app_pages.dart
```

## Naming

| Layer | File | Class |
|-------|------|-------|
| Screen | `home_view.dart` | `HomeView` |
| Controller | `home_controller.dart` | `HomeController` |
| Widget | `custom_button.dart` | `CustomButton` |
| Constants | `app_colors.dart` | `AppColors` |

- Feature folders: `snake_case` (`secret_chats/`, `basic_need/`)
- Routes: constants on `AppPages`; navigate with `Get.toNamed` / `Get.offNamed` / `Get.offAllNamed`
- Screens prefer `GetView<XController>` + `Obx` over new state libraries

## Placement rules

- New screen → `lib/views/<feature>/`
- Reusable UI used in 2+ places → `lib/widgets/<type>/` (not inside a view file)
- One-off private UI → keep in the view file or a private file next to that view
- Colors/assets/spacing → extend existing `core/` helpers; do not add a second source of truth
